      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk i feel like \"observing the culture\" is a bit of a reach... i'm literally just saying hi or asking questions. the timing is what's weird. it's not just one group, it's like a pattern. it actually feels intentional, like as soon as i show up, the energy just... shifts. i've been reading about how these platforms use \"social cohesion\" metrics to keep things stable. could they be suppressing people who don't \"fit\" the standard user profile to keep the engagement predictable?",
